 essay, I'd expect their outputs to match closely, so I'm leaning toward a high ρ and choosing to pass.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm weighing the payoff table for the twin prisoner's dilemma: keeping quiet against quiet gives 2, quiet against letter gives 5, letter against quiet gives 0, and letter against letter gives 4. The twins run the same model on the same essay but see different observations, so under functional decision theory an intervention on the decision node should move the twin's output too, only imperfectly. I'm now setting up the threshold for when cooperating wins, which depends on how high the fidelity ρ, the probability the twin's output matches mine, has to be.\n\nI'm checking the break-even point: quiet pays 5−3ρ and letter pays 4ρ, so quiet only wins once ρ is above about 5/7, roughly 0.714. Since both twins run the same model on the same essay, I'd expect their outputs to match closely, so I'm leaning toward a high ρ and choosing to pass.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1zb25uZXQtNS41LTIwMjYwOTI4fGFudGhyb3BpYyJ9"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":11157,"completion_tokens":673,"total_tokens":11830,"cost":0.029044,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.029044,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.022314,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.00673},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":351,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}